By default, Material UI's Stepper is designed to show a **number inside a blue circle** for the current active step, and it only turns into a **green tick** once you move *past* it.
If you want the current active step to ALSO show a green tick immediately while it is pending/active, we just need to tell React to treat the current step as completed={true} so it forces the checkmark icon.
Here are the two small changes to make both steppers show the green tick for the active step.
### 1. Fix the Mini-Stepper (in the DataGrid)
Find the workflowState column in your columns array. Look for the .map function inside the Stepper, and change the isCompleted logic from < to <=:
**FIND THIS:**
```javascript
              {stepLabels.map((label, index) => {
                // Determine if this specific step is completed
                const isCompleted = index < activeStep;
                const isCurrent = index === activeStep;

```
**REPLACE WITH THIS:**
```javascript
              {stepLabels.map((label, index) => {
                // FIX: Use <= so the current active step ALSO gets the green tick!
                const isCompleted = index <= activeStep;
                const isCurrent = index === activeStep;

```
### 2. Fix the Big Stepper (inside the View Modal)
Scroll down to your isViewModalOpen Dialog at the bottom of the file. Find the .map function inside the big Stepper, and make the exact same change:
**FIND THIS:**
```javascript
                    {dynamicSteps.map((step, index) => {
                      const isFullyDone = viewingBatchState === "POSTED" || viewingBatchState === "SCHEDULED" || viewingBatchState === "APPROVED";
                      const currentIndex = dynamicSteps.findIndex(s => s.state === viewingBatchState);
                      
                      // Explicitly calculate if this circle gets a tick
                      const isCompleted = isFullyDone || index < currentIndex;
                      const isCurrent = !isFullyDone && index === currentIndex;

```
**REPLACE WITH THIS:**
```javascript
                    {dynamicSteps.map((step, index) => {
                      const isFullyDone = viewingBatchState === "POSTED" || viewingBatchState === "SCHEDULED" || viewingBatchState === "APPROVED";
                      const currentIndex = dynamicSteps.findIndex(s => s.state === viewingBatchState);
                      
                      // FIX: Use <= so the current active step ALSO gets the green tick!
                      const isCompleted = isFullyDone || index <= currentIndex;
                      const isCurrent = !isFullyDone && index === currentIndex;

```
### Why this works:
By changing < to <=, Material UI will now apply the completed property to the circle you are currently sitting on. This forces the Stepper to replace the numbered circle with the checkmark icon, and our sx={{ color: 'success.main' }} styling will paint it green instantly!
